<item>
            <title>[IGNITE-4644] Value from IgniteQueue in atomic mode could be lost</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-4644</link>
                <project id="12315922" key="IGNITE">Ignite</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;Assume following case (operations are going concurrently):&lt;br/&gt;
1) Client1 -&amp;gt; offer. Add new index in queue.&lt;br/&gt;
2) On Client1 happens JVM pause or short-time problem with connectivity to cluster longer than 3 sec.&lt;br/&gt;
3) Client2 -&amp;gt; poll. Get index from cache, but no value available.&lt;br/&gt;
4) Client2 checks for value about 3 sec and if no value appears, just skips it.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Should be fixed somehow or make timeout configurable.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
                <environment></environment>
